  "notes": "London self-producer, UK jerk-tagged but self-rejecting the label — mellow cloud-jerk. Soft-knock snares in the \"Headlines\" Drake-school placement over a jerk-ish stutter, mellow hats, restrained subby bass rather than a distorted 808. ⚠ **Its low end is the gentlest in this batch on purpose**: `distortion: none` and a low `slideProb` are what separate a UK cloud-jerk from the US rage cohort it is filed beside. ⚠ Harmony is sample-led and minor/major ambivalent, so the scale weights do not commit to minor. ⚠ Tagged `uk rap` rather than a bare `uk`: a one-word country tag scored above the genre model named `uk-drill` in `lib/fuzzy`, so searching \"uk\" answered an artist instead of the lane.",
